    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-computer-science-and-cybersecurity-radford-virginia-united-states-17661ca6-1fec-4a31-9c2f-642bacb3d8b4": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity - Radford, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity - Radford, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity Radford, Virginia, United States Teaching & Research Faculty Academic Affairs Title: Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity Application Review Date: November 16, 2026 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Radford University’s School of Computing and Information Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in teaching and research, with employment to begin in August 2027. We seek candidates who are passionate about teaching and possess expertise in various subfields of Computer Science, with a focus on applied learning. An ideal candidate will be able to teach in two or more CS areas such as theory, data structures and algorithms, programming languages, software systems, databases, computer networking, cybersecurity, AI / machine learning, or other emerging areas. Candidates are expected to teach and collaborate effectively with individuals from diverse communities and backgrounds. An ideal candidate will also demonstrate enthusiasm and ability to develop a research program that actively engages undergraduate students. The School of Computing and Information Sciences at Radford University offers two undergraduate degree programs: a BS in Computer Science and Technology and a BS in Cybersecurity. The BS in Computer Science and Technology supports five concentrations: Software Engineering, Databases, Networking, Computer Science, and Artificial Intelligence. The Computer Science concentration and the BS in Cybersecurity are both ABET accredited. In addition, Radford University is an NSA Center for Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense Education. The school takes pride in emphasizing hands-on, active learning to develop in-demand skills and knowledge, ensuring graduates are well-prepared for technology careers. Faculty members actively mentor students in research and competitive computing events, including the International Collegiate Programming Contest (ICPC) and various cybersecurity competitions. Required Qualifications • Ph.D. in Computer Science or in a very closely related technical field; applicants with all but their dissertation completed (ABDs) with a planned completion by Summer 2027 will also be considered • An established publication record in the candidate’s research area related to Computer Science Preferred Qualifications: • Ability to integrate AI use-cases into the curriculum of courses they teach • Demonstrated communication skills, preferably in classroom settings, evidenced by prior teaching, lecturing, or teaching assistant (TA) experiences • Demonstrated ability to teach in the core computer science areas • Ability to create hands-on learning exercises or labs for use in teaching • Ability to implement course-based undergraduate research experiences (CUREs) Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must provide the following information: an application cover letter, a current curriculum vitae, and contact information for three (3) professional references including both phone and email addresses for each. Successful candidates will be required to provide official transcripts and will be subject to a criminal background check. Employment Conditions: Radford University is a comprehensive public university of over 7,900 students that has received national recognition for many of its undergraduate and graduate academic programs, as well as its sustainability initiatives. Radford University serves the Commonwealth of Virginia and the nation through a wide range of academic, cultural, human service and research programs. Well known for its strong faculty/student bonds, innovative use of technology in the learning environment and vibrant student life on a beautiful 211-acre American classical campus, Radford University offers students many opportunities to get involved and succeed in and out of the classroom. The University offers 75 bachelor's degree programs in 47 disciplines and six certificates at the undergraduate level; 27 master's programs in 23 disciplines and five doctoral programs at the graduate level; and 21 post-baccalaureate certificates and one post-master's certificate. A Division I member of the NCAA and Big South Conference, Radford University competes in 16 men's and women's varsity athletics. With over 200 clubs and organizations, Radford University offers many opportunities for student engagement, leadership development and community service. In addition to robust academic offerings and engaging student experiences on the main campus located in Radford, Virginia, Radford University also offers a clinical-based educational experience for more than 1,000 students living and learning in Roanoke, Virginia as part of Radford University Carilion, a public-private partnership focused on the cutting-edge delivery of health sciences programming, outreach and service. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position 100% telework: No Months per Year: 9 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Teaching & Research Faculty Employee Classification: Assistant Professor Department: Computing & Info Science, School of Salary: $90,000 - $110,000 (Commensurate with experience, qualifications, and scholarly activity) Department Contact Name: Hwajung Lee Department Contact Phone: 540-831-5238 Department Contact Email: hlee3@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert f9017353 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) c64d9796 Last Name (required) 6b3b11c7 Email (required) 9216b994 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity Provost-E&G Radford University’s School of Computing and Information Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in teaching and research, with employment to begin in August 2027. We seek candidates who are passionate about teaching and possess expertise in various subfields of Computer Science, with a focus on applied learning. Special Purpose Faculty - Marketing Provost-E&G The Department of Marketing in the Davis College of Business and Economics at Radford University invites applications for a full-time Special Purpose faculty appointment in Marketing beginning Spring semester 2027 or Fall semester 2027. Executive Assistant Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a highly organized, discreet, and proactive Executive Assistant to provide executive-level administrative and operational support to the Senior Vice President for Finance and Administration. This position serves as a key liaison between executive leadership, university departments, the Board of Visitors, and external stakeholders. Responsibilities include managing complex calendars and correspondence, preparing confidential documents and reports, coordinating Board of Visitors activities, and supporting financial, budgetary, procurement, and personnel processes. Apply Now First Name (required) f1f9e046 Last Name (required) 9979e1b2 Email (required) 9c810c15 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
