    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/special-purpose-or-tenure-track-faculty-nutrition-and-dietetics-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Special Purpose or Tenure Track Faculty - Nutrition and Dietetics",
      "description": "Special Purpose or Tenure Track Faculty - Nutrition and Dietetics - Radford, Virginia, United States Special Purpose or Tenure Track Faculty - Nutrition and Dietetics - Radford, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Special Purpose or Tenure Track Faculty - Nutrition and Dietetics Radford, Virginia, United States Teaching & Research Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Special Purpose or Tenure Track Faculty - Nutrition and Dietetics Application Review Date: 11/09/2026 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus / Roanoke Campus Job Description Radford University invites applications for a full time faculty position in Foods and Nutrition. The position may be appointed as Special Purpose Faculty or Tenure Track Faculty, depending on the candidate’s qualifications and experience. The faculty member will teach across the Foods and Nutrition curriculum and the ACEND accredited DPD program commencing August 2027. Radford University offers a Bachelor of Science in Foods and Nutrition, including an ACEND accredited Didactic Program in Dietetics (DPD). The program is currently housed in the College of Education and Human Development, with plans to transition to the Waldron College of Health and Human Services by 2030. Responsibilities • Teach undergraduate courses in nutrition, dietetics, and related areas specifically in Food Service and Management, Food Science and Preparation, and Advanced Nutrition & Metabolism • Advise and mentor students through academic and professional development • Provide academic advising • General responsibilities overseeing the teaching kitchen • Provide opportunities for students such as making special contributions toward establishing clinical programs, assisting and supporting students’ scholarly work (e.g., research, creative activities, presentations, and publications) Scholarship/Professional Activities • Engage in professional and/or scholarly activity in the field • Obtains or maintains licensure, certification or similar credentials by accumulating continuing education units or credits. University Service • Participate in service to the department, college, and university Radford University is a comprehensive public university of over 7,900 students that has received national recognition for many of its undergraduate and graduate academic programs, as well as its sustainability initiatives. Radford University serves the Commonwealth of Virginia and the nation through a wide range of academic, cultural, human service and research programs. Well known for its strong faculty/student bonds, innovative use of technology in the learning environment and vibrant student life on a beautiful 211-acre American classical campus, Radford University offers students many opportunities to get involved and succeed in and out of the classroom. The University offers 75 bachelor's degree programs in 47 disciplines and six certificates at the undergraduate level; 27 master's programs in 23 disciplines and five doctoral programs at the graduate level; and 21 post-baccalaureate certificates and one post-master's certificate. A Division I member of the NCAA and Big South Conference, Radford University competes in 16 men's and women's varsity athletics. With over 200 clubs and organizations, Radford University offers many opportunities for student engagement, leadership development and community service. In addition to robust academic offerings and engaging student experiences on the main campus located in Radford, Virginia, Radford University also offers a clinical-based educational experience for more than 1,000 students living and learning in Roanoke, Virginia as part of Radford University Carilion, a public-private partnership focused on the cutting-edge delivery of health sciences programming, outreach and service. Required Qualifications Requirements Special Purpose Faculty: • Education: Earned Master’s degree in Nutrition or closely related discipline. • Experience: Minimum three (3) years of professional experience post credentialing. • Licenses, Certifications and/or Registrations: Interested candidates must hold the Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) credential Requirements for Tenure Track Faculty: • Education: Earned Terminal degree (Ph.D. or nutrition-related practice doctorate) • Experience: Minimum three (3) years of professional experience post credentialing. Experience in teaching college-level classes in traditional classroom and distance education format. Experience with research, publications and other scholarly activity. • Licenses, Certifications and/or Registrations: Interested candidates must hold the Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) credential Preferred Qualifications: • Knowledge of ACEND accreditation standards • Experience teaching at the collegiate level • Experience teaching an accredited DPD program Special Instructions to Applicants Application Procedure: Candidates must submit the following electronically: (1) a letter of application; (2) current and complete curriculum vitae; (3) a one-page philosophy of teaching (4) optional documents that provide evidence of preferred qualifications; (5) names, addresses, email addresses, and telephone numbers of at least three professional/academic references and (6) copies of unofficial transcripts. Additional materials may be requested at a later time. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Employment Conditions: Will be teaching at both the Roanoke and Radford campuses. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position 100% telework: No Months per Year: 9 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Teaching & Research Faculty Employee Classification: Instructor / Assistant Professor Department: Nutrition & Dietetics, Dept of Salary: $52,000 - $65,000 (Commensurate with experience, qualifications, and rank) Department Contact Name: Kathleen Poole Department Contact Phone: 540-831-5305 Department Contact Email: kppoole@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 2a99efa6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Academic Affairs Instructional / 