    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/special-purpose-or-tenure-track-faculty-social-work-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Special Purpose or Tenure-Track Faculty - Social Work",
      "description": "Special Purpose or Tenure-Track Faculty - Social Work - Radford, Virginia, United States Special Purpose or Tenure-Track Faculty - Social Work - Radford, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Special Purpose or Tenure-Track Faculty - Social Work Radford, Virginia, United States Teaching & Research Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Special Purpose or Tenure-Track Faculty - Social Work Application Review Date: 11/10/2026 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Radford University invites applications for the position of Special Purpose Faculty or Tenure-Track Open-Rank Professor in the School of Social Work. This is a nine-month position beginning in August 2027. Special Purpose Faculty Primary responsibilities will be teaching courses in the BSW and MSW programs in both Radford and Roanoke social work program options (includes online and evenings). Special purpose faculty hold continuing, full-time appointments, subject to reappointment every 1-3 years, without eligibility for tenure. Tenure-Track Open-Rank Professor Primary responsibilities will be teaching courses in the BSW and MSW programs in both the Radford and Roanoke social work program options (includes online and evenings), advising, recruitment, university service, and professional contributions. Radford University is a comprehensive public university of over 7,900 students that has received national recognition for many of its undergraduate and graduate academic programs, as well as its sustainability initiatives. Radford University serves the Commonwealth of Virginia and the nation through a wide range of academic, cultural, human service and research programs. Well known for its strong faculty/student bonds, innovative use of technology in the learning environment and vibrant student life on a beautiful 211-acre American classical campus, Radford University offers students many opportunities to get involved and succeed in and out of the classroom. The University offers 75 bachelor's degree programs in 47 disciplines and six certificates at the undergraduate level; 27 master's programs in 23 disciplines and five doctoral programs at the graduate level; and 21 post-baccalaureate certificates and one post-master's certificate. A Division I member of the NCAA and Big South Conference, Radford University competes in 16 men's and women's varsity athletics. With over 200 clubs and organizations, Radford University offers many opportunities for student engagement, leadership development and community service. In addition to robust academic offerings and engaging student experiences on the main campus located in Radford, Virginia, Radford University also offers a clinical-based educational experience for more than 1,000 students living and learning in Roanoke, Virginia as part of Radford University Carilion, a public-private partnership focused on the cutting-edge delivery of health sciences programming, outreach and service. Required Qualifications Special Purpose An MSW from a CSWE-accredited program. Direct practice experience and clinical social work licensure (LCSW). Experience teaching at the university level or providing professional trainings. Tenure-Track Open-Rank Professor A Ph.D. in social work or related field or a DSW, and an MSW from a CSWE-accredited program. ABD candidates whose degree completion is within nine months of the hire date will be considered but will be hired at the rank of Instructor. Preferred Qualifications: Special Purpose Faculty Demonstrated ability to teach clinical social work practice courses and experience with distance education. Interest in or experience with rural health. Tenure-Track Open-Rank Professor Ph.D. in social work, evidence of a scholarly agenda, have experience with distance education, demonstrated ability to teach clinical social work practice courses, interest in or experience with rural health, and at least two years post-MSW social work direct practice experience who are LCSW-eligible. Special Instructions to Applicants All candidates will need to submit an electronic copy of the following: a letter of application, a current curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, contact information of three references within your application. The successful candidate will also be required to provide official transcripts. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position 100% telework: No Months per Year: 9 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Teaching & Research Faculty Department: Social Work, School of Salary: $58,000 - $80,000 (Commensurate with experience, qualifications and rank) Department Contact Name: Andrea Barrick, Ph.D. Department Contact Phone: 540-831-7690 Department Contact Email: asbarrick@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 38b13df1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 729db028 Last Name (required) 5d226bbb Email (required) 21dc72bb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity Provost-E&G Radford University’s School of Computing and Information Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in teaching and research, with employment to begin in August 2027. We seek candidates who are passionate about teaching and possess expertise in various subfields of Computer Science, with a focus on applied learning. Special Purpose Faculty - Marketing Provost-E&G The Department of Marketing in the Davis College of Business and Economics at Radford University invites applications for a full-time Special Purpose faculty appointment in Marketing beginning Spring semester 2027 or Fall semester 2027. Executive Assistant Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a highly organized, discreet, and proactive Executive Assistant to provide executive-level administrative and operational support to the Senior Vice President for Finance and Administration. This position serves as a key liaison between executive leadership, university departments, the Board of Visitors, and external stakeholders. Responsibilities include managing complex calendars and correspondence, preparing confidential documents and reports, coordinating Board of Visitors activities, and supporting financial, budgetary, procurement, and personnel processes. Apply Now First Name (required) d722fc64 Last Name (required) 1f88671c Email (required) 66f5ad0d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
