    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/adjunct-instuctor-dept-of-occupational-therapy-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instuctor - Dept. of Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Adjunct Instuctor - Dept. of Occupational Therapy - Radford, Virginia, United States Adjunct Instuctor - Dept. of Occupational Therapy - Radford, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Instuctor - Dept. of Occupational Therapy Radford, Virginia, United States Adjunct Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Adjunct Instuctor - Dept. of Occupational Therapy Application Review Date: Ongoing review Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Adjunct Faculty positions supplement the faculty of a department wherever additional faculty are needed. Adjunct faculty hold three year appointments, as defined by their letter of appointment without eligibility for tenure; where authorized by the Dean, adjunct appointments may be renewed. Adjunct appointments do not guarantee course assignments. The successful applicant will join the Occupational Therapy Department’s adjunct pool and may have opportunities to teach courses online or in person at our Radford or Roanoke locations. Required Qualifications 1. Hold at least a Masters degree in Occupational Therapy 2. Be currently certified by NBCOT 3. Be eligible for licensure to practice Occupational Therapy in the Commonwealth of Virginia Preferred Qualifications: 1. Clinical experience in OT >3 year 2. Teaching experience in higher education 3. Experience working with underserved, and/or diverse populations 4. Experience as a clinical educator Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit a cover letter, cv and transcripts. Official transcripts will be required of the successful candidate. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position 100% telework: No Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Adjunct Faculty Employee Classification: Part-time Teaching Department: Occupational Therapy, Department of Salary: $2,074.00 (1 credit hour) - $6,222 (3 credit hours) Department Contact Name: Jason Browning Department Contact Phone: 540-831-1948 Department Contact Email: jtbrowning@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1b0078d3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Medical Professionals Instructional / Teaching Faculty Medical Professionals Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 0d7aca60 Last Name (required) 22034628 Email (required) 8875c87e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity Provost-E&G Radford University’s School of Computing and Information Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in teaching and research, with employment to begin in August 2027. We seek candidates who are passionate about teaching and possess expertise in various subfields of Computer Science, with a focus on applied learning. Special Purpose Faculty - Marketing Provost-E&G The Department of Marketing in the Davis College of Business and Economics at Radford University invites applications for a full-time Special Purpose faculty appointment in Marketing beginning Spring semester 2027 or Fall semester 2027. Executive Assistant Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a highly organized, discreet, and proactive Executive Assistant to provide executive-level administrative and operational support to the Senior Vice President for Finance and Administration. This position serves as a key liaison between executive leadership, university departments, the Board of Visitors, and external stakeholders. Responsibilities include managing complex calendars and correspondence, preparing confidential documents and reports, coordinating Board of Visitors activities, and supporting financial, budgetary, procurement, and personnel processes. Apply Now First Name (required) 9706a131 Last Name (required) 172a8c73 Email (required) 051d0905 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most re