    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-biology-roanoke-va-roanoke-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty--Biology Roanoke, VA",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty--Biology Roanoke, VA - Roanoke, Virginia, United States Adjunct Faculty--Biology Roanoke, VA - Roanoke, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty--Biology Roanoke, VA Roanoke, Virginia, United States Adjunct Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Adjunct Faculty--Biology Roanoke, VA Application Review Date: Ongoing review Campus Location: Roanoke Work Authorization: Radford University employs individuals who are legally authorized to work in the United States. Applicants requiring new H-1B visa sponsorship will not be considered. Job Description The Department of Biology is hiring two types of adjunct faculty to teach courses at the Roanoke site for our: 1. Medical Laboratory Science program: Foundations of Medical Laboratory Science (MLAB 401) and Medical Laboratory Science Operations (MLAB 411), or 2. Non-majors: Human Anatomy and Physiology I & II (BIOL 310/BIOL 311) or Microbiology (BIOL 334). Successful applicants will teach the lecture, clinical simulations, or lab components for their courses, all of which will be offered in-person. Instructional responsibilities include (but not limited to) preparing and delivering course content, assessing student learning, holding office hours, and contributing to a rigorous learning environment that focuses on student academic success. The Department of Biology supports and encourages our adjunct faculty to engage in ongoing professional development through their participation in programs, trainings, or seminars offered by Radford’s Center for Innovative Teaching and Learning and by other organizations at Radford University. Adjunct faculty are also highly encouraged to participate in departmental, college, and university events. Required Qualifications All faculty must have at least a Master’s degree in the field/discipline in which they are teaching with 18 hours of course work related to the course(s) being taught. In some cases, subject to the approval by the Provost, a faculty member could be recommended for appointment based on substitution of significant experience for the degree. Clinical Certifications: Candidates applying to teach courses in the Medical Laboratory Science program (i.e., MLAB 401or MLAB 411) must hold a current certification as a Medical Laboratory Scientist. Categorical certifications will not be considered. Candidates must have at least three years’ experience working as a medical laboratory scientist. This certification is not needed if you are applying to teach Anatomy and Physiology or Microbiology. Preferred Qualifications: Prior teaching experience Special Instructions to Applicants Cover Letter: Interested candidates should submit a cover letter introducing who you are as an educator, including: 1. the courses for which you are most prepared to teach in either the Medical Laboratory Science program or for our non-majors, 2. your approach to teaching majors or non-majors with clear examples as evidence, and 3. an explanation for why the Department of Biology at Radford University. Candidates will need to be clear on whether they are applying to teach in the MLS program or applying to teach A&P or Microbiolgy. Your cover letter must be single-spaced, 2-pages maximum, no less than 11-point font, 1-inch margins, and use Times New Roman, Aptos, Arial, or Calibri font. CV and References: Candidates must also submit their curriculum vitae and the names and contact information for three professional references (not part of your letter page limit). Transcripts: Applicants must submit an unofficial copy of transcripts of post-secondary course work with the application. If the applicant’s official transcripts are on file in the Office of the Provost, a statement indicating such, must be submitted in lieu of the documents with the application. Official transcripts of all post-secondary course work will be required upon selection for hire. Official transcripts must be sent directly to the Office of the Provost, Attention: Transcript Clerk/Coordinator, Campus P. O. Box 6910, Radford University, Radford, VA 24142 New Faculty Orientation: Adjunct faculty must attend a scheduled new adjunct faculty orientation as offered upon appointment. The orientation date and time will be announced. Employment Conditions: Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position eligible for telework: No Hours Per Week: As assigned based on teaching schedule per semester. Possible evening courses. Months per Year: Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Adjunct Faculty Normal Work Schedule: Employee Classification: Part-time Teaching Department: Biology, Dept of Salary: $1,385 (1 credit hour) to $5,540 (4 credit hours) Department Contact Name: Dr Matt Close Department Contact Phone: 540-831-5146 Department Contact Email: mclose2@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 95b7cfff Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Academic Affairs Agriculture / Life Science Instructional / Teaching Faculty Academic Affairs Agriculture / Life Science Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Roanoke, Virginia, United States Roanoke, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 7929ec4f Last Name (required) 4699adf3 Email (required) 148b118d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity Provost-E&G Radford University’s School of Computing and Information Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in teaching and research, with employment to begin in August 2027. We seek candidates who are passionate about teaching and possess expertise in various subfields of Computer Science, with a focus on applied learning. Special Purpose Faculty - Marketing Provost-E&G The Department of Marketing in the Davis College of Business and Economics at Radford University invites applications for a full-time Special Purpose faculty appointment in Marketing beginning Spring semester 2027 or Fall semester 2027. Executive Assistant Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a highly organized, discreet, and proactive E