    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-design-special-purpose-or-tenure-track-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Design, Special Purpose or Tenure Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Design, Special Purpose or Tenure Track - Radford, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor - Design, Special Purpose or Tenure Track - Radford, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Design, Special Purpose or Tenure Track Radford, Virginia, United States Teaching & Research Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Professor - Design, Special Purpose or Tenure Track Application Review Date: Ongoing Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description We are looking for a dynamic and creative design educator who can teach in the completely online MFA program in the innovative field of design thinking. Teaching areas are flexible and may include Environment Behavior, Design Thinking, Advanced Design Studios, Teaming, Design Management, Innovation and Creativity, and/or Master’s Thesis Instruction. Candidate should be able to demonstrate innovative thought processes to teach in the completely online MFA program in the field of design thinking. Non-teaching responsibilities include program recruitment, workshop development and implementation, creating sponsored studios and corporate collaborations, national and international marketing, and promotion of design thinking MFA and certificate program. Responsibilities will increase as the program develops. Travel is an expected component of recruitment and professional development. This position requires on-campus interactions and availability 2-3 times per week. The Design Thinking Program is a completely online graduate program. It offer 15 credit certificate program along with a 60 credit MFA terminal degree program. The MFA will augment any bachelor’s or master’s degree by allowing potential students to become leaders in their chosen field. For designers and non-designers, this interdisciplinary, totally online degree will teach in-depth the creative process, creative cognition and environment behavior theories, team development, design management, interactive methodologies and research methodologies. Required Qualifications A minimum of a Masters degree in Instructional Technology, Industrial Design, UX, Business, Design, or other related fields required with professional experience or licensure. Terminal degree and/or PhD preferred. Documented online teaching expertise and experience preferred. Professional certification and/or scholarship in one’s area of expertise and professional practice desirable. Must have the ability to achieve full graduate faculty teaching status and chair thesis committees. Preferred Qualifications: Terminal degree and/or PhD preferred. Documented online teaching expertise and experience preferred. Professional certification and/or scholarship in one’s area of expertise and professional practice desirable. Special Instructions to Applicants All applicants must submit the following: A current resume or curriculum vitae, and a list of three references with names, addresses (including email), and telephone numbers, a 250-word statement on your philosophy of design thinking. Unofficial transcripts will be required of all finalists prior to interview. This is a 12-month position with an anticipated start date of August 2027 Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position eligible for telework: No Hours Per Week: Months per Year: 12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Teaching & Research Faculty Normal Work Schedule: Employee Classification: Assistant Professor, 12 Month Department: Design Thinking Salary: $83,968 - $95,000 Department Contact Name: Holly Cline Department Contact Phone: 5402393559 Department Contact Email: hcline@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 17d1dfba Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Design / Graphic Design / Industrial Design Design / Graphic Design / Industrial Design Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 277ae14f Last Name (required) d4445ddc Email (required) 9a26438b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity Provost-E&G Radford University’s School of Computing and Information Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in teaching and research, with employment to begin in August 2027. We seek candidates who are passionate about teaching and possess expertise in various subfields of Computer Science, with a focus on applied learning. Special Purpose Faculty - Marketing Provost-E&G The Department of Marketing in the Davis College of Business and Economics at Radford University invites applications for a full-time Special Purpose faculty appointment in Marketing beginning Spring semester 2027 or Fall semester 2027. Executive Assistant Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a highly organized, discreet, and proactive Executive Assistant to provide executive-level administrative and operational support to the Senior Vice President for Finance and Administration. This position serves as a key liaison between executive leadership, university departments, the Board of Visitors, and external stakeholders. Responsibilities include managing complex calendars and correspondence, preparing confidential documents and reports, coordinating Board of Visitors activities, and supporting financial, budgetary, procurement, and personnel processes. Apply Now First Name (required) 883b87ea Last Name (required) f80071d2 Email (required) c9b67f8d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-biology-radford-va-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty--Biology Radford, VA",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty--Biology Radford, VA - Radford, Virginia, United States Adjunct Faculty--Biology Radford, VA - Radford, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty--Biology Radford, VA Radford, Virginia, United States Adjunct Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Adjunct Faculty--Biology Radford, VA Application Review Date: Ongoing review Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Adjunct faculty in our department will teach a variety of major and/or non-major courses depending on departmental needs. Examples include Environmental Biology (BIOL 103), Biology for Health Science (BIOL 106/BIOL 106L), Integrative Biology I & II (BIOL 111/BIOL 112), Human Anatomy and Physiology I & II (BIOL 310/BIOL 311), Microbiology (BIOL 334), or a related course in the applicant’s discipline. Successful applicants will teach both the lecture and lab component for their courses, all of which will be offered in-person. Instructional responsibilities include (but not limited to) preparing and delivering course content, assessing student learning, holding office hours, and contributing to a rigorous learning environment that focuses on student academic success. The Department of Biology supports and encourages our adjunct faculty to engage in ongoing professional development through their participation in programs, trainings, or seminars offered by Radford's Center for Innovative Teaching and Learning and by other organizations at Radford University. Adjunct faculty are also highly encouraged to participate in departmental, college, and university events. Required Qualifications All faculty must have at least a Master’s degree in the field/discipline in which they are teaching with 18 hours of course work related to the course(s) being taught. In some cases, subject to the approval by the Provost, a faculty member could be recommended for appointment based on substitution of significant experience for the degree. Preferred Qualifications: Prior teaching experience Special Instructions to Applicants Cover Letter: Interested candidates should submit a cover letter introducing who you are as an educator, including: - the courses for which you are most prepared to or are highly interested in teaching from the list provided, - your approach to teaching majors and non-majors with clear examples as evidence, and - an explanation for why the Department of Biology at Radford University. Your cover letter must be single-spaced, 2-pages maximum, no less than 11-point font, 1-inch margins, and use Times New Roman, Aptos, Arial, or Calibri font. CV and References: Candidates must also submit their curriculum vitae and the names and contact information for three professional references (not part of your letter page limit). Transcripts: Applicants must submit an unofficial copy of transcripts of post-secondary course work with the application. If the applicant’s official transcripts are on file in the Office of the Provost, a statement indicating such, must be submitted in lieu of the documents with the application. Official transcripts of all post-secondary course work will be required upon selection for hire. Official transcripts must be sent directly to the Office of the Provost to the following address. Attention: Transcript Clerk/Coordinator Campus P. O. Box 6910 Radford University Radford, VA 24142 New Faculty Orientation: Adjunct faculty must attend a scheduled new adjunct faculty orientation as offered upon appointment. The orientation date and time will be announced. Employment Conditions: Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position eligible for telework: No Hours Per Week: As assigned based on teaching schedule per semester. Possible evening courses. Months per Year: Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Adjunct Faculty Normal Work Schedule: Employee Classification: Part-time Teaching Department: Biology, Dept of Salary: $1,385 (1 credit hour) to $5,540 (4 credit hours) Department Contact Name: Dr. Matt Close Department Contact Phone: 540-831-5146 Department Contact Email: mclose2@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert d224a8ab Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Radford, Virginia, United States Radford, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 44d65d52 Last Name (required) c6a37df5 Email (required) f30a2f85 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity Provost-E&G Radford University’s School of Computing and Information Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in teaching and research, with employment to begin in August 2027. We seek candidates who are passionate about teaching and possess expertise in various subfields of Computer Science, with a focus on applied learning. Special Purpose Faculty - Marketing Provost-E&G The Department of Marketing in the Davis College of Business and Economics at Radford University invites applications for a full-time Special Purpose faculty appointment in Marketing beginning Spring semester 2027 or Fall semester 2027. Executive Assistant Finance & Administration-E&G Radford University is seeking a highly organized, discreet, and proactive Executive Assistant to provide executive-level administrative and operational support to the Senior Vice President for Finance and Administration. This position serves as a key liaison between executive leadership, university departments, the Board of Visitors, and external stakeholders. Responsibilities include managing complex calendars and correspondence, preparing confidential documents and reports, coordinating Board of Visitors activities, and supporting financial, budgetary, procurement, and personnel processes. Apply Now First Name (required) 99a6e025 Last Name (required) d2bdf7c2 Email (required) 4d060a3e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and it