    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-design-online-other-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Design Online",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Design Online - Other, Virginia, United States Adjunct Faculty - Design Online - Other, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Design Online Other, Virginia, United States Adjunct Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Adjunct Faculty - Design Online Application Review Date: immediately Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Work Authorization: Radford University employs individuals who are legally authorized to work in the United States. Applicants requiring new H-1B visa sponsorship will not be considered. Job Description The Department of Design welcomes applications for adjunct teaching online for our Design Thinking certificate and MFA program. Positioned may be needed a variety of areas related to Human Centered Design, Design Thinking, Empathy, Design Thinking Studios, Environment Design, Design Management, Story Telling, Collaboration, Research Methods, Instructional Design, etc. Adjunct Faculty positions supplement the faculty of a department wherever additional faculty are needed. Adjunct faculty hold, as defined by their letter of appointment, without eligibility for tenure; where authorized by the Dean, adjunct appointments may be renewed. Adjunct appointments do not guarantee course assignments. Specific responsibilities of adjunct faculty are given in their letter of appointment. The specific starting and expiration dates for appointments are noted in their letter of appointment. Primary responsibilities include teaching in the area of the candidate’s specialization. Adjunct faculty shall be evaluated in every course, including summer sessions. Required Qualifications All faculty must have at least a Master's degree in the field/discipline in which they are teaching, with 18 hours of coursework related to the course(s) being taught. In some cases, subject to the approval by the Provost, a faculty member could be recommended for appointment based on the substitution of experience for the degree. Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience teaching. Prior design industry experience and or licensing and certifications. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must submit an unofficial copy of their transcripts of post-secondary courses with the application. If the applicant’s official transcripts are on file in the Office of the Provost, a statement indicating such, must be submitted in lieu of the documents with the application. Please note that the Office of the Provost only has access to transcripts from previous faculty employment and those are only retained for 5 years after initial departure from Radford University. Official transcripts of all post-secondary coursework will be required upon selection for hire. Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position eligible for telework: Yes Hours Per Week: Varies depending on courses taught Months per Year: 9-12 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Adjunct Faculty Normal Work Schedule: Varies depending on courses taught and possible weekends Department: Design Thinking Salary: $1,295 (1 credit hour) to $3,885 (3 credit hours) Department Contact Name: Holly Cline Department Contact Phone: 540-831-5932 Department Contact Email: hcline@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 0c069749 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost-E&G Provost-E&G Categories Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Academic Affairs Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Other, Virginia, United States Other, Virginia, United States First Name (required) 30574146 Last Name (required) f89e8158 Email (required) 99a3d27c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Assistant Professor - Computer Science and Cybersecurity Provost-E&G Radford University’s School of Computing and Information Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in teaching and research, with employment to begin in August 2027. We seek candidates who are passionate about teaching and possess expertise in various subfields of Computer Science, with a focus on applied learning. Special Purpose Faculty - Marketing Provost-E&G The De