      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Health and Human Performance - Radford, Virginia, United States Adjunct Faculty - Health and Human Performance - Radford, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Health and Human Performance Radford, Virginia, United States Adjunct Faculty Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Title: Adjunct Faculty - Health and Human Performance Application Review Date: Ongoing review Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Work Authorization: Radford University employs individuals who are legally authorized to work in the United States. Applicants requiring new H-1B visa sponsorship will not be considered. Job Description Teach courses in one of the following areas: Allied Health Science, Health and Exercise Science, Physical and Health Education, Sport Management, and Nutrition and Dietetics. Required Qualifications All faculty must have at least a Master's degree in the field/discipline in which they teach, with 18 hours of coursework related to the course(s) they teach. In some cases, subject to the Provost's approval, a faculty member may be recommended for appointment based on substituting significant experience for the degree. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in exercise, health, or sport-related fields. Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must submit an unofficial copy of their post-secondary transcripts with the application. If the applicant's official transcript is on file with the Office of the Provost, a statement indicating this must be submitted with the application in lieu of the documents. Official transcripts of all post-secondary coursework will be required upon selection for hire. Official transcripts must be sent directly to the Office of the Provost, Attention: Transcript Clerk/Coordinator, Campus PO Box 6910, Radford University, Radford, VA 24142 Adjunct Instructors must attend a scheduled adjunct orientation as offered upon appointment. Orientation date and time will be announce