    "https://jobs.radford.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-sound-design-technical-direction-radford-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Sound Design/Technical Direction",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Sound Design/Technical Direction - Radford, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor, Sound Design/Technical Direction - Radford, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Sound Design/Technical Direction Radford, Virginia, United States Teaching & Research Faculty Academic Affairs Title: Assistant Professor, Sound Design/Technical Direction Application Review Date: November 22, 2026 Campus Location: Radford City - Main Campus Job Description Assistant Professor, Full-time/Tenure Track 9-month faculty position in Sound Design/Technical Direction, beginning Fall 2027. The successful candidate is a congenial collaborator and mentor with strong oral and written communication skills. This position is supported by a 12-month full-time faculty Assistant Technical Director/Scene Shop Manager. Duties (include but are not limited to): •Performing Technical Director duties for department productions •Designing sound and/or mentoring student sound designers for department productions •Teaching courses in Sound Design, Sound Engineering, and/or Technical Production •Support the Assistant Technical Director/Scene Shop Manager in the supervision of work study students •Advising, committee service and recruitment, as assigned Required Qualifications •Terminal degree in technical direction and/or sound design •Undergraduate teaching experience •Sound design experience, including live sound reinforcement and experience with QLab and Dante •Technical experience in scenic construction including but not limited to metalwork, welding, foam sculpting and wood •Proficiency in Vectorworks or other CAD software •Advanced knowledge of stage rigging and structural analysis •Strong time, budgeting, and personnel management skills Preferred Qualifications: •Expertise in projection and/or media production •Experience with CNC Mills and Scenic Automation •OSHA safety training and/or ETCP certification in Theatre Rigging Special Instructions to Applicants Submit electronically: • Cover letter, CV, teaching philosophy, and sample syllabi • Names and phone numbers of three references • Digital portfolio or a link to portfolio website Is this position Grant Funded: No Is this position restricted: No Is this position 100% telework: No Months per Year: 9 Statement of Economic Interest Required: No FLSA Status: Exempt Work Classification: Teaching & Research Faculty Normal Work Schedule: Employee Classification: Assistant Professor Department: Theatre, Dept of Salary: $55,000 - $72,000 Department Contact Name: Robyn Berg Department Contact Phone: 5408315231 Department Contact Email: rberg3@radford.edu Equal Opportunity Statement: Radford University does not discriminate with regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, disability, age, veteran status, national origin, religion, or political affiliation in the administration of its educational programs, activities, admission or employment practices. Clery Statement In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Radford University publishes an Annual Security and Fire Safety Report. The report includes the university’s policies, procedures, and programs concerning safety and security, as well as three years’ of crime statistics for our campus. As a prospective employee, you are entitled to a copy of this report. The report and statistical data can be found online at Radford.edu/police. You may also request a paper copy of the report from the Radford University Police Department located at 810 East Main Street PO Box 6883, Radford, VA, 24142. Reasonable Accommodation Statement If you are an individual with a disability and desire accommodation in the application process please contact the hiring department. Criminal Background Check Statement Radford University is committed to ensuring a safe and secure environment for all employees, students, volunteers, and stakeholders. As part of our hiring and screening process, we conduct criminal background checks in compliance with Virginia Code § 19.2-389 and other applicable state and federal laws. Successful candidates will be required to have a criminal background check. Apply now! Similar Jobs Education Support Specialist Provost-E&G Come join our team! The Office of Graduate Affairs at Radford University seeks a student-centered Education Support Specialist to provide comprehensive student services and operational support for approximately 2,000 active graduate students across more than 47 graduate programs. This position collaborates with academic departments and university offices to resolve student concerns, streamline processes, and support graduate student retention and success. The ideal candidate demonstrates strong communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills, along with a commitment to student advocacy and collaborative service. Special Purpose Faculty, Sport Management Provost-E&G Radford University invites applications for a full time special purpose faculty position in Sport Management. Administrative Assistant Provost-E&G The Physician Assistant Studies at Radford University invites applicants for an Administrative Assistant position. Multitasking ability, budget management, significant computer skills, and attention to detail required. Please see full description for details. Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
